WEBVTT

00:16.640 --> 00:19.470
I never dreamed before

00:19.470 --> 00:22.310
I'm gonna knock the door

00:22.310 --> 00:25.880
into the world of perfect free

00:25.880 --> 00:27.980
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:27.980 --> 00:30.820
You're gonna say I'm lying

00:30.820 --> 00:33.550
I'm gonna get the chance

00:33.550 --> 00:37.120
I thought a chance is far from me

00:37.120 --> 00:38.290
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:38.290 --> 00:41.200
I was made to hit in America

00:41.200 --> 00:44.060
(I was made to hit in America)

00:44.060 --> 00:49.970
I was made to hit in America

00:49.970 --> 00:53.640
You are the sun, you are the star

00:53.640 --> 00:55.640
(To me, forever)

00:55.640 --> 00:59.350
You are the sun, you are the star

00:59.350 --> 01:02.580
(To me, forever)

01:09.420 --> 01:15.030
I was made to hit in America

01:15.030 --> 01:17.870
I was made to hit in America

01:17.870 --> 01:20.730
(I was made to hit in America)

01:20.730 --> 01:23.540
I was made to hit in America

01:23.540 --> 01:26.310
(I was made to hit in America)

01:26.310 --> 01:34.180
I was made to hit in America

01:50.730 --> 01:54.100
Let's start getting back to our hotel.

01:57.640 --> 02:01.140
You're right. This place
looks kinda dangerous.

02:01.140 --> 02:03.680
Say, look!

02:03.680 --> 02:05.780
That dog...

02:05.780 --> 02:09.450
Yeah! It looks just like Ryusuke-kun's dog!

02:09.450 --> 02:12.650
-Hey! Let's get a picture!
-Yeah!

02:17.930 --> 02:19.690
It's coming this way!

02:19.690 --> 02:22.490
-I'm scared!
-Kii-chan, watch out!

02:25.430 --> 02:28.460
-He's gonna maul us to death!
-Yo! Keith!

02:29.700 --> 02:31.570
Keith, what's the matter with you, man!

02:31.570 --> 02:35.340
Getting all bloodied and chasing chicks
up and down the street, man!

02:35.340 --> 02:37.810
Just gotta be careful with women!

02:40.950 --> 02:42.250
We're in trouble!

02:42.250 --> 02:45.120
"Broadcast in the School"

02:45.120 --> 02:47.250
"Broadcast in the School"

02:45.120 --> 02:47.250
And then?

02:47.250 --> 02:50.260
They took all our money, of course!

02:50.260 --> 02:52.830
And we walked back to the hotel.

02:52.830 --> 02:55.300
It was a miracle we made it home!

02:55.300 --> 02:57.960
I'll say!

02:57.960 --> 03:00.760
And this is the dog's photo.

03:01.940 --> 03:05.340
Imagine, coming across a dog
that looks like Beck.

03:08.780 --> 03:10.910
So blurry I can't make any sense of it!

03:10.910 --> 03:13.610
Huh? Oh, come on!

03:13.610 --> 03:17.420
I'm going to the convenience store
to get toshikoshi noodles.

03:17.420 --> 03:19.190
-We really saw it!
-Yeah!

03:19.190 --> 03:22.090
Well, anyway, at least you're okay.

03:36.670 --> 03:39.830
Oww! Hot!

03:55.120 --> 03:58.660
I pray that Hyodo's not in my class!

03:58.660 --> 04:00.130
"Fortune"

04:01.660 --> 04:04.130
"Temporary danger
followed by peace of mind."

04:07.070 --> 04:08.970
Yes!

04:40.400 --> 04:41.990
"March"
"In Jamaica until the 20th"

04:42.340 --> 04:45.770
The old lady went to Jamaica this time?

04:51.210 --> 04:53.410
(Graduation Song)

04:58.790 --> 05:00.420
Today, you graduate
from East Ihara Middle School.

05:00.420 --> 05:03.390
"Graduation"

05:00.420 --> 05:03.390
Today, you graduate
from East Ihara Middle School.

05:03.390 --> 05:05.230
Today, you graduate
from East Ihara Middle School.

05:05.230 --> 05:11.630
Use what you have learned at
this school to move to the next level.

05:11.630 --> 05:15.930
And please remember, you are not alone...

05:24.810 --> 05:26.510
Izumi-chan...

05:26.510 --> 05:28.750
Hurry!

05:28.750 --> 05:29.780
Sorry! Sorry!

05:29.780 --> 05:31.050
Izumi-chan!

05:31.050 --> 05:33.650
Hey, what's with your melon roll?!

05:33.650 --> 05:34.720
Hyodo!

05:34.720 --> 05:40.130
The sugar coating's all melted!
This isn't a melon roll!

05:40.130 --> 05:42.860
Sorry. The usual bakery was closed...

05:42.860 --> 05:46.470
Huh?! Whatever. Go buy another one.

05:46.470 --> 05:47.800
Okay...

05:51.140 --> 05:53.110
Tanaka-kun!

05:54.210 --> 05:56.710
"Saito Paper Company"

05:54.210 --> 05:56.710
Are you going to your part-time job now?

05:56.710 --> 05:59.480
"Saito Paper Company"

05:59.480 --> 06:00.810
"Saito Paper Company"

05:59.480 --> 06:00.810
How do you do?

06:00.810 --> 06:02.680
"Saito Paper Company"

06:00.810 --> 06:02.680
I'm Ogasawara, Tanaka-kun's
substitute homeroom teacher.

06:02.680 --> 06:06.920
I'm Ogasawara, Tanaka-kun's
substitute homeroom teacher.

06:06.920 --> 06:09.910
You're Saito-san...right?

06:12.160 --> 06:16.090
You can call me Kenichi!

06:17.500 --> 06:20.860
Oh, let me make you some tea!

06:31.240 --> 06:34.810
A part-time job? Don't be silly.

06:34.810 --> 06:37.880
I'm just a crazy middle-aged man
who's teaching Yukio-kun

06:37.880 --> 06:41.690
how to swim and play the guitar for free.

06:41.690 --> 06:44.890
I see. But what a relief.

06:44.890 --> 06:48.290
I'm glad you have such
a good friend, Tanaka-kun!

06:52.970 --> 06:57.940
Koyuki-kun...That Momoko-sensei
is really a nice teacher...

06:57.940 --> 07:03.000
Kenichi Saito, age 44. Very discerning.
Unattached and independent.

07:08.150 --> 07:11.020
I hope everyone here spent
the holiday in a worthwhile manner.

07:11.020 --> 07:13.150
"School Entrance Ceremony"

07:11.020 --> 07:13.150
I hope everyone here spent
the holiday in a worthwhile manner.

07:13.150 --> 07:17.020
"School Entrance Ceremony"

07:13.150 --> 07:17.020
We start a new school year today.
At this time of year...

07:17.020 --> 07:21.530
"Grade 9A"

07:17.020 --> 07:21.530
We start a new school year today.
At this time of year...

07:21.530 --> 07:24.830
I will be the homeroom teacher
for 9th grade, group 1.

07:24.830 --> 07:29.800
My name is Eiji Oikawa. I'm looking
forward to this year with you.

07:29.800 --> 07:35.470
My forte is imitating Mick Jagger.
That's where you laugh.

07:46.920 --> 07:49.790
Hey, Tanaka...He knows.

07:51.730 --> 07:57.130
Someone snitched to Rikiya-kun
that you busted up the Jaguar.

07:57.130 --> 07:59.700
And now I'm tangled up in this.

07:59.700 --> 08:01.470
I see...

08:01.470 --> 08:04.600
Can you get 50,000 yen in three days?

08:04.600 --> 08:06.670
I-I don't think so.

08:06.670 --> 08:11.010
He wants 100,000. I'll get 50,000 somehow.

08:11.950 --> 08:15.480
-You have that much?
-Idiot! I'll get it somehow!

08:15.480 --> 08:16.680
Somehow?

08:16.680 --> 08:19.290
Do something within three days!

08:19.290 --> 08:22.250
I'm serious; it's your fault
if he kills you!

08:23.960 --> 08:26.860
50,000 yen...in three days?

08:27.830 --> 08:29.690
That's impossible...

08:31.100 --> 08:34.620
The White Falcon...
the ultimate Gretsch guitar.

08:35.900 --> 08:39.610
It's the pride and joy of my collection.

08:39.610 --> 08:43.240
I'll let you borrow this, Koyuki-kun.
For as long as you like.

08:44.340 --> 08:46.610
Huh?! Are you serious?!

08:46.610 --> 08:50.080
You always work hard for me.

08:50.080 --> 08:51.280
Saito-san!

08:51.280 --> 08:58.590
And...I've been thinking it'd be nice
to see Momoko-sensei again...

08:58.590 --> 09:00.180
I'm counting on you.

09:12.110 --> 09:13.900
Ryusuke-kun...

09:16.740 --> 09:18.370
Koyuki...

09:20.910 --> 09:23.250
That guitar...

09:23.250 --> 09:26.850
This is a White Falcon.

09:26.850 --> 09:32.630
Oh? It's called the
most beautiful guitar in the world.

09:32.630 --> 09:33.960
Where are you-

09:33.960 --> 09:39.970
I'm going to the studio
for practice. Wanna come?

09:39.970 --> 09:41.160
Yes!

09:49.380 --> 09:53.450
All right, our time is limited.
Let's get started, Koyuki.

09:53.450 --> 09:55.780
Huh? Me too?!

09:55.780 --> 09:57.550
You can play, right?

10:37.860 --> 10:40.450
Thanks for today! See you later!

10:42.160 --> 10:45.860
-He's really been practicing.
-Yeah.

10:47.770 --> 10:51.340
He's far past a first-year beginner.

10:51.340 --> 10:53.540
Yeah, I agree.

10:53.540 --> 10:56.700
And he has a feel for the music.

11:09.790 --> 11:11.460
Hey, Tanaka...

11:11.460 --> 11:13.560
Are you making a fool of me?

11:13.560 --> 11:16.330
That's all I could make from
selling my games and comics!

11:16.330 --> 11:18.830
Do something by tomorrow's deadline.

11:18.830 --> 11:22.030
We're talking about Rikiya-kun here!

11:24.800 --> 11:29.870
Saito-san! Please do something
about this pile of sex magazines!

11:31.110 --> 11:33.110
These magazines are proof

11:33.110 --> 11:35.250
that I've lived through
the Showa and Heisei eras!

11:35.250 --> 11:39.050
But you can't live in the past like this.

11:39.050 --> 11:42.420
Momoko-sensei won't like you...

11:43.790 --> 11:46.290
Let's take these to the dump!

11:46.290 --> 11:47.760
Huh?!

11:53.400 --> 11:53.870
This is that
super-famous star, Miho Nakama!

11:53.870 --> 11:57.170
"Miho Nakama on a tropical island"

11:53.870 --> 11:57.170
This is that
super-famous star, Miho Nakama!

11:57.170 --> 11:58.000
"Miho Nakama on a tropical island"

11:58.000 --> 12:00.170
"Miho Nakama on a tropical island"

11:58.000 --> 12:00.170
Koyuki-kun! H-hurry!

12:00.170 --> 12:00.730
Koyuki-kun! H-hurry!

12:01.470 --> 12:05.340
"Used Books Store"

12:11.350 --> 12:13.410
W-wow!

12:14.420 --> 12:18.990
46,500 yen? This isn't enough.

12:18.990 --> 12:20.830
I can't get any more.

12:20.830 --> 12:25.600
Shit! It's the deadline,
so I'll give it to Rikiya-kun,

12:25.600 --> 12:29.300
but don't blame me for
whatever happens to you.

12:30.200 --> 12:31.690
Cripes!

12:43.120 --> 12:46.880
-It's Rikiya-sempai!
-What? He already graduated!

12:50.660 --> 12:52.280
Move! You're in the way!

12:55.830 --> 12:59.990
-Yamada! Where the hell is he?
-Hello!

13:01.000 --> 13:07.370
Idiot! Do you know how much
I begged Rikiya-kun, dumbass?

13:07.370 --> 13:08.940
I'm sorry.

13:08.940 --> 13:11.600
Damn right!

13:15.780 --> 13:17.880
Something's not right...

13:27.160 --> 13:30.360
Hold it! Time out!

13:31.200 --> 13:34.330
Koyuki. Listen to the drums.

13:51.420 --> 13:54.690
-Hey, look at those two.
-Huh?

13:54.690 --> 13:58.690
They've been awfully
close lately, those two.

13:58.690 --> 14:04.230
Hey, don't rub it in. This guy
worries more than you think.

14:04.230 --> 14:07.170
By the way, have you heard the New Order?

14:07.170 --> 14:07.770
Huh?

14:07.770 --> 14:09.970
That's why I hate the Japanese!

14:09.970 --> 14:12.810
That kind of thinking
won't get you anywhere!

14:12.810 --> 14:14.840
You're Japanese, Maho!

14:14.840 --> 14:18.510
-Shut up! That doesn't matter!
-What about Do Division?
-Yeah. How about Happy Mondays?

14:18.510 --> 14:22.170
-You can't just say no to everything!
-I'm not saying that!
-Yeah, New Wave, right?

14:24.750 --> 14:26.550
Hey, Koyuki...

14:29.160 --> 14:31.490
-Take this.
-What is it?

14:35.290 --> 14:40.770
Ryusuke-kun! Hey! Wait!

14:40.770 --> 14:42.330
Sorry to keep you waiting!

14:44.770 --> 14:47.970
-What's the matter?
-Nothing...

14:49.580 --> 14:53.880
-Something happen with my brother?
-No, nothing...

14:53.880 --> 14:54.510
"Minami"

14:54.510 --> 14:56.350
"Minami"
What a huge house!

14:56.350 --> 14:57.050
What a huge house!

14:57.050 --> 15:00.350
It's not like I built it.

15:00.350 --> 15:04.120
I heard Taira-kun talking about you.

15:04.120 --> 15:08.330
He said, "Koyuki's progress is amazing.
Like cotton absorbing water."

15:08.330 --> 15:12.020
Huh? Was that an impression of Taira-kun?

15:13.570 --> 15:19.970
But everyone's so slow.
I knew you had talent ages ago.

15:19.970 --> 15:22.780
Oh, thanks...

15:22.780 --> 15:25.110
It'll be done copying in a little bit.

15:28.510 --> 15:30.980
Huh? Something wrong?

15:30.980 --> 15:35.320
Err, no...Oh yeah, I gotta
pay you for the minidisc.

15:37.320 --> 15:39.550
-You dropped something.
-Huh?

15:42.560 --> 15:45.900
No, it's not what you-!

15:49.770 --> 15:52.760
Where'd you get that from?!

15:54.010 --> 15:56.670
My head still throbs...

15:57.980 --> 16:01.210
What if I wind up dying?

16:07.720 --> 16:10.060
-There's this movie I wanna see...
-Yes?

16:10.060 --> 16:12.050
Are you free this Sunday?

16:15.430 --> 16:17.590
Oh, that uniform!

16:19.630 --> 16:22.000
-See you tomorrow!
-All right!

16:24.370 --> 16:27.740
Oh, Koyuki! Hiya!

16:27.740 --> 16:31.540
Izumi-chan...Who was that just now?

16:31.540 --> 16:36.080
-An upperclassman in my club.
-Oh, I see...

16:36.080 --> 16:37.750
Is he-?

16:37.750 --> 16:40.080
He said he wants to go out with me.

17:27.530 --> 17:32.060
If I walk around like this in a daze...
life is gonna just pass me by!

17:46.250 --> 17:48.520
Whoa, how awful!

17:54.930 --> 17:58.260
'Morning, Kojima-kun!
About the book I lent you-

18:00.270 --> 18:02.360
Kigata-kun, I was thinking...

18:04.270 --> 18:06.400
Hey, Tanabe...

18:16.150 --> 18:18.210
Yeah, and then...

18:25.390 --> 18:27.330
Hey, shape up!

18:30.530 --> 18:33.260
You asked me for a copy...

18:34.470 --> 18:35.930
"Broadcasting"

18:34.470 --> 18:35.930
"Media Room"

18:42.910 --> 18:45.410
What's that?

18:45.410 --> 18:48.610
-What's this broadcast?
-It's American music.

18:48.610 --> 18:51.020
Yeah...

18:51.020 --> 18:52.580
This song...

18:55.050 --> 18:57.020
Hey, open up!

18:57.020 --> 19:00.090
If you don't open up now,
it'll go on your school record!

19:00.090 --> 19:02.130
Hear that?!

19:02.130 --> 19:05.770
-Huh?! It's Tanaka!
-Tanaka-kun!

19:05.770 --> 19:07.500
Open up!

19:07.500 --> 19:09.740
-Hey, Tanaka!
-Cut this out!

19:09.740 --> 19:14.370
-Tanaka!
-Tanaka-kun!

19:14.370 --> 19:16.680
-Man, it's so loud!
-What a racket!

19:16.680 --> 19:19.410
-But I like this song!
-It's not bad.

19:19.410 --> 19:21.380
This song's pretty good.

19:21.380 --> 19:23.850
Yeah...But man, it's taking you long!

19:33.790 --> 19:34.760
"Faculty Office"

19:34.760 --> 19:36.660
"Faculty Office"

19:34.760 --> 19:36.660
-Now tell me.
-Yes...

19:36.660 --> 19:37.500
"Faculty Office"

19:36.660 --> 19:37.500
Why would an earnest student
like you do such a thing?

19:37.500 --> 19:41.400
Why would an earnest student
like you do such a thing?

19:41.400 --> 19:45.810
-Do you watch movies?
-Not too much. Why?

19:45.810 --> 19:48.510
An innocent man who is
wrongly sent to prison

19:48.510 --> 19:52.750
plays an opera that he loves in prison.

19:52.750 --> 19:57.450
And the rest of the inmates
feel freedom for just a moment.

19:57.450 --> 19:59.150
There was a scene like that.

19:59.150 --> 20:03.290
Huh? This isn't prison!

20:03.290 --> 20:06.030
That was Dying Breed's "50 Cent Wisdom."

20:06.030 --> 20:08.260
That was a great choice!

20:08.260 --> 20:12.500
-Who are you?
-Yuji Sakurai, Grade 9B.

20:12.500 --> 20:15.900
Do you play an instrument, Tanaka-kun?

20:15.900 --> 20:19.440
Sakurai-kun...You probably
shouldn't talk to me.

20:19.440 --> 20:21.370
Huh? Why not?

20:21.370 --> 20:25.310
Someone bad has it in for me...

20:25.310 --> 20:30.210
-Who's that?
-Some weird transfer student.

20:36.290 --> 20:39.760
Hey, transfer student.
Come to the back of the campus.

20:39.760 --> 20:43.090
We'll teach you how things are done
at East Ihara Middle School.

20:44.600 --> 20:47.730
I see. So you're the Hyodo Gang.

20:47.730 --> 20:50.870
The culprits who make life
at school miserable.

20:50.870 --> 20:52.670
You cocky bastard!

20:54.710 --> 20:56.710
Why you-!

20:56.710 --> 20:58.470
Bastard!

21:03.720 --> 21:05.340
Tanaka-kun!

21:06.590 --> 21:07.850
Your face!

21:07.850 --> 21:12.190
I wanted to give this to you.
It's Dying Breed's Germany concert.

21:13.190 --> 21:15.060
Sakurai-kun...

21:17.260 --> 21:20.930
I told you it was bad to talk to me...

21:20.930 --> 21:25.600
Did you read the Eddie Lee
interview in Guitar World?

21:25.600 --> 21:30.740
Yeah. Eddie's Telecaster was cool.

21:30.740 --> 21:33.650
There are two types of people in this world.

21:33.650 --> 21:35.150
Huh?

21:35.150 --> 21:38.250
Clever people and obedient people.

21:38.250 --> 21:45.420
Clever people think man-made laws
and morals make the world work.

21:45.420 --> 21:49.160
But I don't bother with any of that.

21:49.160 --> 21:51.200
Eddie is amazing, huh?

21:51.200 --> 21:52.790
Oww!

21:55.840 --> 21:58.700
Won't you come see
our band practice sometime?

21:58.700 --> 22:01.700
So you're in a band?

22:30.540 --> 22:36.040
Ryusuke said earlier that he wants
to make the band's sound hotter.

22:36.040 --> 22:39.370
He intends to bring Koyuki into Beck...

22:51.390 --> 22:53.490
Another minute

22:53.490 --> 22:56.190
Feelin' so fine

22:58.500 --> 23:00.730
You turn the freeze

23:00.730 --> 23:03.460
into warm light

23:05.570 --> 23:09.140
Had a premonition

23:09.140 --> 23:11.840
I've been waitin' ever since

23:11.840 --> 23:15.350
My world comin' down

23:15.350 --> 23:18.140
It's got me spinnin' 'round

23:19.920 --> 23:26.090
If you really wanna fly

23:26.090 --> 23:28.850
you gotta let go

23:41.110 --> 23:43.440
Simply the most

23:43.440 --> 23:45.480
big sensation

23:45.480 --> 23:48.280
(once you're here you won't go back)

23:48.280 --> 23:50.550
She's really pretty

23:50.550 --> 23:52.550
One-eyed vision

23:52.550 --> 23:55.390
(lose the fear it don't come back)

23:55.390 --> 23:58.890
Little sister showed me

23:58.890 --> 24:01.560
Really took me for a ride

24:01.560 --> 24:03.230
My world comin' down

24:03.230 --> 24:06.560
(once you're here you won't go back)

24:06.560 --> 24:10.590
(lose the fear it don't come back)

24:14.940 --> 24:17.240
I had such a shock recently.

24:17.240 --> 24:17.410
"Next Episode"

24:17.240 --> 24:17.410
"Eve of the Live Show"

24:17.240 --> 24:17.410
I had such a shock recently.

24:17.410 --> 24:21.170
"Next Episode"

24:17.410 --> 24:21.170
"Eve of the Live Show"

24:17.410 --> 24:21.170
A girl told me...that my feet stink!
